BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
45 780 Td
(   3. Referring Secondary Parameters to Primary Side:) Tj
T*
(   - Transformation ratio: K = N2 / N1.) Tj
T*
(   - Secondary current referred to primary: I2' = K * I2.) Tj
T*
(   - Secondary voltage referred to primary: V2' = V2 / K.) Tj
T*
(   - To preserve identical I^2*R copper loss and I^2*X reactive VAR drops:) Tj
T*
(   \(I2'\)^2 * R2' = I2^2 * R2 => \(K * I2\)^2 * R2' = I2^2 * R2 => R2' = R2 / K^2.) Tj
T*
(   Similarly: X2' = X2 / K^2.) Tj
T*
(   4. Total Equivalent Parameters Referred to Primary:) Tj
T*
(   - Equivalent resistance: R_eq1 = R1 + R2' = R1 + R2 / K^2.) Tj
T*
(   - Equivalent leakage reactance: X_eq1 = X1 + X2' = X1 + X2 / K^2.) Tj
T*
(   - Equivalent impedance: Z_eq1 = sqrt\( R_eq1^2 + X_eq1^2 \).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(>> Solution to Question 3:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain Open-Circuit \(OC\) and Short-Circuit \(SC\) tests on a single-phase transformer, detailing how equivalent circuit parameters are extracted.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Open-Circuit and Short-Circuit Tests on Transformers:) Tj
T*
(   1. Open-Circuit \(No-Load\) Test:) Tj
T*
(   - Objective: Determine core \(iron\) loss Pi, no-load parameters Rc and Xm.) Tj
T*
(   - Procedure: Low-voltage \(LV\) winding is energized at rated voltage V1 and rated frequency f;) Tj
T*
(   high-voltage \(HV\) winding is left strictly open-circuited.) Tj
T*
(   - Instrument Readings: Voltmeter reads rated voltage V1; Ammeter reads no-load current I0;) Tj
T*
(   Wattmeter reads no-load power W0.) Tj
T*
(   - Parameter Extraction:) Tj
T*
(   * Since no-load current is small \(2-5%\), primary copper loss I0^2*R1 is negligible; hence W0 =) Tj
T*
(   Core Loss Pi.) Tj
T*
(   * No-load power factor: cos\(phi0\) = W0 / \(V1 * I0\).) Tj
T*
(   * Core loss current: Iw = I0 * cos\(phi0\) => Shunt core resistance: Rc = V1 / Iw.) Tj
T*
(   * Magnetizing current: Im = I0 * sin\(phi0\) = sqrt\(I0^2 - Iw^2\) => Magnetizing reactance: Xm =) Tj
T*
(   V1 / Im.) Tj
T*
(   2. Short-Circuit \(Impedance\) Test:) Tj
T*
(   - Objective: Determine full-load copper loss P_cu, equivalent resistance R_eq, and leakage) Tj
T*
(   reactance X_eq.) Tj
T*
(   - Procedure: LV winding is short-circuited with a thick conductor; a reduced variable voltage) Tj
T*
(   V_sc \(approx 5-10% of rated\) is applied to HV winding until rated full-load current I_sc flows.) Tj
T*
(   - Instrument Readings: V_sc, I_sc, and short-circuit power W_sc.) Tj
T*
(   - Parameter Extraction:) Tj
T*
(   * Because applied voltage V_sc is tiny, core flux is tiny \(Phi proportional to V_sc\); iron) Tj
T*
(   losses are negligible.) Tj
T*
(   * W_sc equals full-load copper loss P_cu.) Tj
T*
(   * Equivalent resistance: R_eq = W_sc / I_sc^2.) Tj
T*
(   * Equivalent impedance: Z_eq = V_sc / I_sc.) Tj
T*
(   * Equivalent leakage reactance: X_eq = sqrt\( Z_eq^2 - R_eq^2 \).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(>> Solution to Question 4:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Derive the mathematical expression for Voltage Regulation of a transformer, analyzing lagging, leading, and unity power factor conditions.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Voltage Regulation of a Transformer:) Tj
T*
(   1. Definition:) Tj
T*
(   - Defined as the fractional change in secondary terminal voltage from no-load to full-load,) Tj
T*
(   expressed as a percentage of rated full-load voltage:) Tj
T*
ET

