(>> Solution to Question 5:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Derive the condition for Maximum Efficiency in a power transformer, and contrast power transformer design with distribution transformer design.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Transformer Efficiency Optimization and Transformer Design Philosophies:) Tj
T*
(   1. Derivation of Maximum Efficiency Condition:) Tj
T*
(   - Output active power: P_out = V2 * I2 * cos\(phi\).) Tj
T*
(   - Total losses: Total Losses = Iron Loss Pi + Copper Loss P_cu = Pi + I2^2 * R_eq2.) Tj
T*
(   - Efficiency formula:) Tj
T*
(   eta = P_out / \(P_out + Losses\) = \(V2 * I2 * cos\(phi\)\) / [ V2 * I2 * cos\(phi\) + Pi + I2^2 *) Tj
T*
(   R_eq2 ].) Tj
T*
(   - Dividing numerator and denominator by I2:) Tj
T*
(   eta = \(V2 * cos\(phi\)\) / [ V2 * cos\(phi\) + Pi / I2 + I2 * R_eq2 ].) Tj
T*
(   - For constant V2 and load power factor cos\(phi\), eta is maximized when denominator D is) Tj
T*
(   minimized:) Tj
T*
(   d\(D\) / d\(I2\) = - Pi / I2^2 + R_eq2 = 0 => Pi / I2^2 = R_eq2 => Pi = I2^2 * R_eq2 = P_cu.) Tj
T*
(   - Fundamental Rule: Maximum efficiency occurs at the operating load where Variable Copper Loss) Tj
T*
(   equals Constant Core \(Iron\) Loss:) Tj
T*
(   P_cu = Pi.) Tj
T*
(   - Load fraction x_max for peak efficiency:) Tj
T*
(   x_max = sqrt\( Pi / P_cu_full_load \).) Tj
T*
(   2. Power Transformer versus Distribution Transformer Design:) Tj
T*
(   - Power Transformers: Installed at generating stations and transmission substations; operated) Tj
T*
(   continuously at near 100% full rated load. Designed to have maximum efficiency at 90-100% full) Tj
T*
(   load. Core losses and copper losses are balanced at rated output.) Tj
T*
(   - Distribution Transformers: Installed on local utility poles/substations directly serving) Tj
T*
(   domestic/commercial consumers. Load varies widely over 24 hours \(average load ~40-60%\). Core) Tj
T*
(   remains energized 24/7 regardless of load. Designed with low core flux density and high-grade) Tj
T*
(   silicon steel to minimize constant iron loss, achieving maximum efficiency at 50-70% load to) Tj
T*
(   maximize All-Day Energy Efficiency \(kWh\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET

