12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the construction, working principle, and copper saving of an Autotransformer compared to a conventional two-winding transformer.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Autotransformer Theory and Copper Saving:) Tj
T*
(   1. Construction and Operating Principle:) Tj
T*
(   - Unlike a conventional transformer with two electrically isolated windings, an autotransformer) Tj
T*
(   uses a single continuous tapped winding wound on a laminated iron core.) Tj
T*
(   - A portion of the winding is common to both primary and secondary circuits.) Tj
T*
(   - Power is transferred between circuits via two simultaneous mechanisms:) Tj
T*
(   \(a\) Inductive \(Electromagnetic Induction\) through mutual flux;) Tj
T*
(   \(b\) Conductive \(Direct Electrical Conduction\) through physical galvanic contact.) Tj
T*
(   2. Copper Saving Derivation:) Tj
T*
(   - Weight of copper winding is proportional to \(Number of Turns * Conductor Cross-Sectional) Tj
T*
(   Area\), which is proportional to Turns * Current \(Ampere-Turns\):) Tj
T*
(   Weight proportional to N * I.) Tj
T*
(   - Two-Winding Transformer:) Tj
T*
(   Weight W2 = c * \(N1 * I1 + N2 * I2\), where c is a constant.) Tj
T*
(   Since N1 * I1 approx N2 * I2: W2 = 2 * c * N1 * I1.) Tj
T*
(   - Autotransformer \(Step-Down, N1 > N2, V1 > V2\):) Tj
T*
(   Section AB \(N1 - N2 turns\) carries current I1.) Tj
T*
(   Common Section BC \(N2 turns\) carries difference current \(I2 - I1\).) Tj
T*
(   Weight Wa = c * [ \(N1 - N2\) * I1 + N2 * \(I2 - I1\) ].) Tj
T*
(   Substitute transformation ratio K = N2 / N1 = I1 / I2 \(K < 1\):) Tj
T*
(   Wa = c * [ N1*I1 - N2*I1 + N2*I2 - N2*I1 ] = c * [ 2*N1*I1 - 2*N2*I1 ] = 2*c*N1*I1 * [ 1 -) Tj
T*
(   N2/N1 ] = W2 * \(1 - K\).) Tj
T*
(   - Ratio of Copper Weights:) Tj
T*
(   Wa / W2 = 1 - K.) Tj
T*
(   - Copper Saved:) Tj
T*
(   Delta-W = W2 - Wa = K * W2.) Tj
T*
(   - Conclusion: Copper saving is directly proportional to transformation ratio K. When K is close) Tj
T*
(   to unity \(e.g., K = 0.9, stepping 230 V to 207 V\), copper savings reach 90%!) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
