(   [Problem Statement]: Derive the generated EMF and developed Torque equations of a DC Machine from Lorentz Force and Faraday's Law.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   EMF and Torque Equations of DC Machines:) Tj
T*
(   1. Generated EMF Equation:) Tj
T*
(   - Let P = number of poles, Phi = flux per pole \(Webers\), Z = total number of active armature) Tj
T*
(   conductors, N = armature rotational speed in rpm, A = number of parallel paths.) Tj
T*
(   - Flux cut by a single conductor in one complete revolution:) Tj
T*
(   d\(Phi\) = P * Phi.) Tj
T*
(   - Time taken for one revolution:) Tj
T*
(   dt = 60 / N seconds.) Tj
T*
(   - Average EMF induced in one conductor by Faraday's law:) Tj
T*
(   e_avg = d\(Phi\) / dt = \(P * Phi\) / \(60 / N\) = \(P * Phi * N\) / 60 Volts.) Tj
T*
(   - The Z conductors are divided into A parallel paths; hence each path contains \(Z / A\)) Tj
T*
(   conductors in series:) Tj
T*
(   Eg = e_avg * \(Z / A\) = \(Phi * Z * N * P\) / \(60 * A\) Volts.) Tj
T*
(   - For Lap Winding \(A = P\): Eg = \(Phi * Z * N\) / 60.) Tj
T*
(   - For Wave Winding \(A = 2\): Eg = \(Phi * Z * N * P\) / 120.) Tj
T*
