(   [Problem Statement]: Compare DC Shunt, Series, and Compound Motors regarding torque-speed characteristics and industrial applications.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Comparative Analysis of DC Motors:) Tj
T*
(   1. DC Shunt Motor:) Tj
T*
(   - Circuit: Field winding connected in parallel with armature across supply V. Field current If) Tj
T*
(   = V / Rsh is constant; hence field flux Phi is constant.) Tj
T*
(   - Torque Relation: T proportional to Ia. Speed relation: N proportional to \(V - Ia*Ra\) / Phi.) Tj
T*
(   - Characteristic: Speed drops only marginally \(3-5%\) from no-load to full-load due to tiny) Tj
T*
(   Ia*Ra drop. Excellent speed regulation \('constant-speed motor'\).) Tj
T*
(   - Applications: Lathe machines, centrifugal pumps, fans, blowers, machine tools, printing) Tj
T*
