(   2. DC Series Motor:) Tj
T*
(   - Circuit: Field winding connected in series with armature, carrying full armature current: Phi) Tj
T*
(   proportional to Ia \(below saturation\).) Tj
T*
(   - Torque Relation: T proportional to Phi * Ia proportional to Ia^2 \(quadratic starting torque\).) Tj
T*
(   - Speed Relation: N proportional to \(V - Ia*\(Ra + Rse\)\) / Phi approx 1 / Ia.) Tj
T*
(   - Characteristic: At light load \(Ia -> 0\), Phi -> 0 and speed N skyrockets toward dangerous) Tj
T*
(   runaway levels. Must NEVER be run without mechanical load! High torque at low speeds.) Tj
T*
(   - Applications: Electric locomotives \(railway traction\), cranes, hoists, trolley buses,) Tj
T*
(   automobile self-starters.) Tj
T*
(   3. Cumulative Compound Motor:) Tj
T*
(   - Circuit: Contains both series and shunt field windings assisting each other.) Tj
T*
(   - Characteristic: High starting torque \(from series field\) combined with safe, stable no-load) Tj
T*
(   speed limiting \(from shunt field\).) Tj
T*
(   - Applications: Heavy stamping presses, rolling mills, shears, reciprocating compressors,) Tj
T*
(   elevators.) Tj
