(   1. Stator Spatial and Temporal Winding Architecture:) Tj
T*
(   - Stator carries three identical phase windings \(R, Y, B\) physically displaced in space around) Tj
T*
(   the stator bore by 120 electrical degrees.) Tj
T*
(   - Windings are energized by balanced 3-phase sinusoidal currents displaced in time by 120) Tj
T*
(   electrical degrees:) Tj
T*
(   i_R\(t\) = Im * sin\(omega * t\)) Tj
T*
(   i_Y\(t\) = Im * sin\(omega * t - 120 deg\)) Tj
T*
(   i_B\(t\) = Im * sin\(omega * t - 240 deg\)) Tj
T*
(   2. Resulting Fluxes:) Tj
T*
(   - Each phase current establishes a pulsating, stationary sinusoidal flux along its magnetic) Tj
T*
(   axis:) Tj
T*
(   Phi_R = Phi_m * sin\(omega * t\)) Tj
T*
(   Phi_Y = Phi_m * sin\(omega * t - 120 deg\)) Tj
T*
(   Phi_B = Phi_m * sin\(omega * t - 240 deg\)) Tj
T*
(   3. Mathematical Derivation of Net Resultant Flux \(Phi_res\):) Tj
T*
(   - Resolve fluxes along orthogonal horizontal \(X\) and vertical \(Y\) axes:) Tj
T*
(   Phi_x = Phi_R + Phi_Y * cos\(120 deg\) + Phi_B * cos\(240 deg\)) Tj
T*
(   = Phi_m * [ sin\(wt\) - 0.5 * sin\(wt - 120\) - 0.5 * sin\(wt - 240\) ] = 1.5 * Phi_m * sin\(omega *) Tj
T*
(   t\).) Tj
T*
(   Phi_y = 0 + Phi_Y * sin\(120 deg\) - Phi_B * sin\(120 deg\)) Tj
T*
(   = Phi_m * \(sqrt\(3\)/2\) * [ sin\(wt - 120\) - sin\(wt - 240\) ] = - 1.5 * Phi_m * cos\(omega * t\).) Tj
T*
(   - Net Flux Magnitude:) Tj
T*
(   |Phi_res| = sqrt\( Phi_x^2 + Phi_y^2 \) = 1.5 * Phi_m * sqrt\( sin^2\(wt\) + cos^2\(wt\) \) = 1.5 *) Tj
T*
(   Phi_m = Constant!) Tj
T*
(   - Spatial Angular Orientation:) Tj
T*
(   theta = arctan\( Phi_y / Phi_x \) = - omega * t.) Tj
T*
(   4. Physical Conclusion:) Tj
T*
(   - The resultant magnetic flux has a strictly constant magnitude equal to 1.5 times the maximum) Tj
T*
(   peak flux of an individual phase \(1.5 * Phi_m\).) Tj
T*
(   - Its spatial orientation rotates uniformly in space at synchronous speed Ns = \(120 * f\) / P) Tj
T*
(   rpm.) Tj
T*
