(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the Synchronous Motor working principle, why it is not self-starting, and methods used to start it.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Synchronous Motor Fundamentals and Starting Methods:) Tj
T*
(   1. Working Principle and Magnetic Interlocking:) Tj
T*
(   - Stator carries 3-phase winding fed by AC, generating a rotating magnetic field at synchronous) Tj
T*
(   speed Ns.) Tj
T*
(   - Rotor carries salient or cylindrical field poles energized with DC excitation, producing) Tj
T*
(   fixed magnetic North and South poles.) Tj
T*
(   - Operation requires magnetic interlocking between opposite stator and rotor poles. Once) Tj
T*
(   locked, rotor is dragged around in perfect synchronism at exactly Ns = \(120 * f\) / P under all) Tj
T*
(   loads up to pull-out torque.) Tj
T*
(   2. Why Synchronous Motors are NOT Self-Starting:) Tj
T*
(   - At standstill, rotor has zero rotational speed. The stator RMF sweeps past rotor poles at) Tj
T*
(   1500/3000 rpm.) Tj
T*
(   - During the first half-cycle, stator North pole attracts rotor South pole, exerting forward) Tj
T*
(   torque.) Tj
T*
(   - Exactly a half-cycle later \(10 milliseconds at 50 Hz\), the stator pole reverses to South,) Tj
T*
(   repelling the rotor South pole with equal backward torque.) Tj
T*
(   - Due to large rotor mechanical inertia, the rotor cannot accelerate from rest in 10 ms; net) Tj
T*
(   average starting torque is identically ZERO.) Tj
T*
(   3. Starting Methods:) Tj
T*
(   - Damper Windings \(Amortisseur Windings\): Heavy copper bars short-circuited by end rings) Tj
T*
(   embedded in rotor pole faces. Motor starts as an induction motor. Near Ns \(~95% speed\), DC) Tj
T*
(   field is switched on; magnetic pull pulls rotor into synchronism.) Tj
T*
(   - Auxiliary Pony Motor: Small induction motor accelerates synchronous rotor up to synchronous) Tj
T*
(   speed prior to energizing DC excitation.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
