(   [Problem Statement]: Explain V-Curves and Inverted V-Curves of Synchronous Motors, detailing the operation of a Synchronous Condenser.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   V-Curves, Inverted V-Curves, and Synchronous Condensers:) Tj
T*
(   1. Physical Mechanism of Field Variation:) Tj
T*
(   - In a synchronous motor connected to infinite bus V running at constant mechanical shaft load:) Tj
T*
(   V = Ef /_ -delta + Ia * Zs.) Tj
T*
(   - Active power P = \(V * Ef / Xs\) * sin\(delta\) = Constant; hence \(Ef * sin delta\) is constant.) Tj
T*
(   2. V-Curves \(Armature Current Ia vs Field Current If\):) Tj
T*
(   - Under-Excited \(Low If, Ef < V\): Motor draws lagging reactive power to support its magnetic) Tj
T*
(   field. Stator current Ia is high and lagging \(cos phi < 1.0\).) Tj
T*
(   - Normal Excitation: Ef matches bus requirement. Motor operates at Unity Power Factor \(cos phi) Tj
T*
