(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the Scott Connection \(T-Connection\) of transformers for 3-Phase to 2-Phase conversion, deriving turns ratios.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Scott Connection \(T-Connection\) for Phase Transformation:) Tj
T*
(   1. Purpose:) Tj
T*
(   - Interconnects a balanced 3-phase supply with a 2-phase load \(or vice versa\), commonly used in) Tj
T*
(   electric arc furnaces and electric railways.) Tj
T*
(   2. Configuration:) Tj
T*
(   - Uses two single-phase transformers:) Tj
T*
(   \(a\) Main Transformer: Connected across lines B and C of 3-phase supply \(V_BC = V_L /_ 0 deg\).) Tj
T*
(   Primary winding has N1 turns with a 50% center tap \(point D\).) Tj
T*
(   \(b\) Teaser Transformer: One primary terminal connected to phase line A; the other terminal) Tj
T*
(   connected to center tap D of main transformer.) Tj
T*
(   3. Mathematical Derivation of Voltage and Turns:) Tj
T*
(   - Line voltage V_BC = V_L.) Tj
T*
(   - Potential at center tap D is midpoint of V_B and V_C: V_D = 0.5 * \(V_B + V_C\).) Tj
T*
(   - Voltage across teaser primary \(V_AD\):) Tj
T*
(   From equilateral voltage triangle: V_AD = V_A - V_D = V_L * [ sqrt\(3\) / 2 ] = 0.866 * V_L.) Tj
T*
(   - Teaser voltage is in exact quadrature \(90 degrees displaced\) with main voltage V_BC.) Tj
T*
(   - To produce equal secondary voltages \(V2_main = V2_teaser\) with identical secondary turns N2,) Tj
T*
(   the primary turns of the teaser must equal:) Tj
T*
(   N_teaser = \(sqrt\(3\) / 2\) * N1 = 0.866 * N1.) Tj
T*
(   - Teaser primary is tapped at exactly 86.6% of main transformer turns.) Tj
T*
(   4. Secondary Voltages:) Tj
T*
(   - Secondary windings of main and teaser produce two isolated single-phase voltages equal in) Tj
T*
(   magnitude and strictly 90 degrees out of phase, forming an ideal balanced 2-phase system.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
