(   2. Rotor Power Breakdown:) Tj
T*
(   - In rotor equivalent circuit, rotor resistance R2/s is divided into:) Tj
T*
(   R2 / s = R2 + R2 * [ \(1 - s\) / s ].) Tj
T*
(   - The first term R2 represents physical Rotor Copper Loss:) Tj
T*
(   P_rcu = 3 * I2^2 * R2 = s * P_ag.) Tj
T*
(   - The second term R2 * \(1 - s\)/s represents Internal Gross Mechanical Power Developed:) Tj
T*
(   P_mech = 3 * I2^2 * R2 * [ \(1 - s\) / s ] = \(1 - s\) * P_ag.) Tj
T*
(   3. Fundamental Power Ratio:) Tj
T*
(   P_ag : P_rcu : P_mech = 1 : s : \(1 - s\).) Tj
T*
(   4. Shaft Useful Output Power:) Tj
T*
(   - P_shaft = P_mech - \(Mechanical Friction and Windage Losses + Stray Load Losses\).) Tj
T*
(   - Electromagnetic torque developed: T_e = P_ag / omega_s = P_mech / omega_r.) Tj
