12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the phenomena of Cogging and Crawling in 3-Phase Induction Motors and how they are eliminated.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Cogging and Crawling in Induction Motors:) Tj
T*
(   1. Crawling:) Tj
T*
(   - Physical Cause: Stator windings distributed in discrete slots produce space harmonic MMF) Tj
T*
(   waves in addition to fundamental flux. Odd harmonics \(3rd, 5th, 7th, 11th...\) are present.) Tj
T*
(   - 3rd harmonics cancel in 3-phase systems.) Tj
T*
(   - 5th harmonic rotates backward at Ns/5, producing braking torque.) Tj
T*
(   - 7th harmonic rotates forward at Ns/7, producing a positive torque hump around Ns/7.) Tj
T*
(   - Motor Behavior: Under heavy inertia, the motor can get trapped and run stable at) Tj
T*
(   approximately 1/7th of synchronous speed with loud growling noise \('crawling'\).) Tj
T*
(   - Remedy: Use fractional-pitch \(chorded\) and skewed stator/rotor windings to suppress 7th) Tj
T*
(   harmonic MMF.) Tj
T*
(   2. Cogging \(Magnetic Locking\):) Tj
T*
(   - Physical Cause: Occurs when the number of stator slots Ss is equal to or an exact integer) Tj
T*
(   multiple of rotor slots Sr \(Ss = k * Sr\).) Tj
T*
(   - At standstill, stator tooth faces align directly opposite rotor tooth faces, creating paths) Tj
T*
(   of minimum magnetic reluctance.) Tj
T*
(   - The magnetic reluctance force resists rotor acceleration, causing the rotor to lock) Tj
T*
(   magnetically into the stator and refuse to start \('cogging'\).) Tj
T*
(   - Remedy: Ensure stator and rotor slot numbers are coprime \(Ss != Sr\); skew rotor conductor) Tj
T*
(   slots by one stator slot pitch.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
