(   [Problem Statement]: Explain Field-Oriented Control \(Vector Control\) of 3-Phase Induction Motors, covering Clarke and Park transformations.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Field-Oriented Control \(FOC\) of Induction Motors:) Tj
T*
(   1. Operational Philosophy:) Tj
T*
(   - In DC motors, field flux \(produced by field winding\) and torque \(produced by armature) Tj
T*
(   current\) are naturally decoupled and perpendicular.) Tj
T*
(   - In AC induction motors, stator current simultaneously controls both flux and torque, making) Tj
T*
(   high-dynamic control complex.) Tj
T*
(   - FOC transforms 3-phase AC motor dynamics into an equivalent separately excited DC motor) Tj
T*
(   model.) Tj
T*
(   2. Mathematical Coordinate Transformations:) Tj
T*
(   - Clarke Transformation \(3-phase stationary abc to 2-phase stationary alpha-beta\):) Tj
T*
