/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain Doubly-Fed Induction Generators \(DFIG\) in wind energy conversion systems, detailing sub-synchronous and super-synchronous operation.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Doubly-Fed Induction Generator \(DFIG\) in Wind Turbines:) Tj
T*
(   1. System Configuration:) Tj
T*
(   - Stator is connected directly to the 3-phase 50/60 Hz utility grid.) Tj
T*
(   - Rotor is connected to the grid through slip rings and a back-to-back bidirectional PWM) Tj
T*
(   converter \(Rotor-Side Converter [RSC] + DC Link + Grid-Side Converter [GSC]\).) Tj
T*
(   - Converter rating is only ~25-30% of total machine rating, drastically reducing cost and) Tj
T*
(   footprint compared to full-scale converters.) Tj
T*
(   2. Operating Regimes across Slip:) Tj
T*
(   - Sub-Synchronous Mode \(Wind speed low, rotor speed N < Ns, slip s > 0\):) Tj
T*
(   Stator feeds power to grid. Rotor absorbs electrical slip power from grid via converter:) Tj
T*
(   P_rotor = s * P_ag into rotor.) Tj
T*
(   - Synchronous Mode \(N = Ns, s = 0\):) Tj
T*
(   Operates as a synchronous generator. Rotor fed with pure DC from converter.) Tj
T*
(   - Super-Synchronous Mode \(High wind speed, rotor speed N > Ns, slip s < 0\):) Tj
T*
(   Both stator AND rotor deliver power to the grid simultaneously! Total electrical output:) Tj
T*
(   P_total = P_stator + |P_rotor| = P_ag + |s| * P_ag.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
