/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain Transformer Inrush Current, deriving the mathematical formula for flux doubling and analyzing protection measures.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Transformer Magnetizing Inrush Current and Harmonic Restraint:) Tj
T*
(   1. Analytical Derivation of Flux Doubling:) Tj
T*
(   - When an unloaded transformer is energized at t = 0 by sinusoidal voltage v\(t\) = Vm *) Tj
T*
(   sin\(omega * t + alpha\):) Tj
T*
(   Core flux: Phi\(t\) = \(1 / N\) * Integral v\(t\) dt = - \(Vm / omega*N\) * cos\(omega*t + alpha\) + C.) Tj
T*
(   - Let switching occur at voltage zero-crossing \(alpha = 0\) with zero initial remanent flux:) Tj
T*
(   Phi\(0\) = 0 => 0 = - Phi_m + C => C = Phi_m.) Tj
T*
(   - Instantaneous core flux:) Tj
T*
(   Phi\(t\) = Phi_m * [ 1 - cos\(omega * t\) ].) Tj
T*
(   - At half-cycle \(omega*t = pi\):) Tj
T*
(   Phi_peak = 2 * Phi_m.) Tj
T*
(   - If residual flux Phi_r exists from prior tripping:) Tj
T*
ET

