/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain Stepper Motors: Variable Reluctance, Permanent Magnet, and Hybrid types, deriving step angle.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Stepper Motor Architectures and Stepping Mechanics:) Tj
T*
(   1. Operational Principle:) Tj
T*
(   - An electromechanical actuator that converts digital electrical pulses into discrete, precise) Tj
T*
(   angular displacements \(steps\).) Tj
T*
(   2. Step Angle Formula:) Tj
T*
(   - Step angle: beta = [ \(Ns - Nr\) / \(Ns * Nr\) ] * 360 degrees = 360 / \(m * Nr\), where Ns =) Tj
T*
(   stator teeth, Nr = rotor teeth, m = number of phases.) Tj
T*
(   3. Types of Stepper Motors:) Tj
T*
(   - Variable Reluctance \(VR\) Stepper: Soft iron multi-toothed rotor with zero permanent magnets.) Tj
T*
(   Rotor aligns with stator teeth to minimize magnetic circuit reluctance. Operates on reluctance) Tj
T*
(   torque.) Tj
T*
(   - Permanent Magnet \(PM\) Stepper: Rotor consists of a cylindrical permanent magnet with) Tj
T*
(   alternating N-S poles. Higher detent torque and magnetic holding torque.) Tj
T*
(   - Hybrid Stepper: Combines VR and PM principles. Rotor has an axial permanent magnet sandwiched) Tj
T*
(   between two soft iron toothed end-caps \(one end magnetized all North, other end all South\).) Tj
T*
(   Achieves ultra-fine step angles \(e.g., 1.8 deg, 0.9 deg\) with high torque and high stepping) Tj
T*
(   rates.) Tj
T*
(   4. Drive Modes: Wave drive \(single-phase ON\), Full-step drive \(two phases ON\), Half-step drive,) Tj
T*
(   and Microstepping \(sinusoidal PWM current control\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
