(   [Problem Statement]: Explain Brushless DC \(BLDC\) Motors, including electronic commutation, Hall sensors, and inverter topologies.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Brushless DC \(BLDC\) Motor Engineering:) Tj
T*
(   1. Architecture:) Tj
T*
(   - Inside-out construction relative to brushed DC machines:) Tj
T*
(   * Stator: 3-phase distributed or concentrated windings wound on laminated steel core.) Tj
T*
(   * Rotor: High-energy permanent magnets \(Neodymium-Iron-Boron, NdFeB\) mounted on surface or) Tj
T*
(   interior.) Tj
T*
(   2. Electronic Commutation:) Tj
T*
(   - Eliminates mechanical commutator and carbon brushes \(zero sparking, zero brush wear, low) Tj
T*
(   acoustic noise, maintenance-free, efficiency > 90%\).) Tj
T*
(   - Commutation is executed electronically using a 3-phase full-bridge inverter \(6) Tj
T*
(   MOSFETs/IGBTs\).) Tj
T*
(   3. Rotor Position Sensing:) Tj
T*
(   - Three Hall effect sensors spaced 120 or 60 electrical degrees apart detect rotor magnetic) Tj
T*
(   pole transitions.) Tj
T*
