/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Analyze Electrical Machine Losses and derive the separation of Eddy Current and Hysteresis losses from experimental data.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Loss Separation in Ferromagnetic Cores:) Tj
T*
(   1. Core Loss Formulation:) Tj
T*
(   - Total Iron Loss: Pi = P_h + P_e.) Tj
T*
(   - Steinmetz Hysteresis Loss: P_h = k_h * f * B_m^n \(where n approx 1.6 to 2.0\).) Tj
T*
(   - Eddy Current Loss: P_e = k_e * f^2 * B_m^2 * t^2 \(where t is lamination thickness\).) Tj
T*
(   2. Experimental Separation Procedure:) Tj
T*
(   - Keep maximum flux density B_m constant by maintaining constant V / f ratio.) Tj
T*
(   - Total core loss equation simplifies to:) Tj
T*
(   Pi = A * f + B * f^2, where A = k_h * B_m^n and B = k_e * B_m^2 * t^2.) Tj
T*
(   - Divide through by frequency f:) Tj
T*
(   \(Pi / f\) = A + B * f.) Tj
T*
(   - Measure total core loss Pi at multiple frequencies \(e.g., 25 Hz, 40 Hz, 50 Hz, 60 Hz\).) Tj
T*
(   - Plot \(Pi / f\) along Y-axis versus f along X-axis:) Tj
T*
(   * The plot yields a straight line with slope B and Y-intercept A.) Tj
T*
(   - Hysteresis loss at frequency f1: P_h1 = A * f1.) Tj
T*
(   - Eddy current loss at frequency f1: P_e1 = B * f1^2.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
