/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Analyze the Starting Methods of 3-Phase Squirrel-Cage Induction Motors \(DOL, Star-Delta, Auto-Transformer, Soft Starters\).) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Comparison of Induction Motor Starting Methods:) Tj
T*
(   1. Direct-On-Line \(DOL\) Starter:) Tj
T*
(   - Motor connected directly across full line voltage.) Tj
T*
(   - Starting Current: I_st = 5 to 7 times rated full-load current \(I_fl\).) Tj
T*
(   - Starting Torque: T_st / T_fl = \(I_st / I_fl\)^2 * s_fl.) Tj
T*
(   - Severe voltage dip on utility supply; suitable only for small motors \(< 5 kW\).) Tj
T*
(   2. Star-Delta Starter:) Tj
T*
(   - Windings connected in Star during starting, switched to Delta at ~80% rated speed.) Tj
T*
(   - Starting Voltage per phase: V_st = V_L / sqrt\(3\).) Tj
T*
(   - Starting Current: I_st_star = \(1/3\) * I_st_delta.) Tj
T*
(   - Starting Torque: T_st_star = \(1/3\) * T_st_delta.) Tj
T*
(   - Reduces both starting current and starting torque to exactly 33.3% of DOL values.) Tj
T*
(   3. Auto-Transformer Starter:) Tj
T*
(   - Motor energized via autotransformer taps \(tapping ratio x, typically 0.5, 0.65, 0.8\).) Tj
T*
(   - Starting Voltage: V_st = x * V_L.) Tj
T*
(   - Starting Current drawn from line: I_line = x^2 * I_st_DOL.) Tj
T*
(   - Starting Torque: T_st = x^2 * T_st_DOL.) Tj
T*
(   - Flexible starting torque selection.) Tj
T*
(   4. Electronic Soft Starter:) Tj
T*
(   - Utilizes back-to-back thyristors \(SCRs\) to smoothly ramp stator voltage from initial preset) Tj
T*
(   value up to full voltage, eliminating all mechanical and electrical starting surges.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
