(>> Solution to Question 28:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain Permanent Magnet Synchronous Motors \(PMSM\), comparing Surface PMSM \(SPMSM\) with Interior PMSM \(IPMSM\).) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Permanent Magnet Synchronous Motors \(PMSM\):) Tj
T*
(   1. Construction and Features:) Tj
T*
(   - Stator: 3-phase sinusoidal distributed winding.) Tj
T*
(   - Rotor: High-remanence NdFeB permanent magnets.) Tj
T*
(   - Driven by sinusoidal PWM inverter \(produces zero torque ripple when back-EMF is purely) Tj
T*
(   sinusoidal\).) Tj
T*
(   2. Surface-Mounted PMSM \(SPMSM\):) Tj
T*
(   - Magnets glued onto the outer cylindrical surface of rotor core.) Tj
T*
(   - Because relative permeability of magnets is near unity \(mu_r approx 1.0, same as air\), the) Tj
T*
(   effective magnetic air-gap is large and uniform around the circumference.) Tj
T*
(   - Direct-axis inductance equals quadrature-axis inductance: Ld = Lq.) Tj
T*
(   - Zero reluctance torque; torque is produced exclusively by permanent magnet flux interaction:) Tj
T*
(   T = 1.5 * \(P/2\) * Psi_m * iqs.) Tj
T*
(   3. Interior PMSM \(IPMSM\):) Tj
T*
(   - Magnets buried deeply inside rotor lamination steel slots.) Tj
T*
(   - Rotor steel provides low-reluctance paths along q-axis; hence Lq > Ld!) Tj
T*
(   - Develops both PM alignment torque AND significant reluctance torque:) Tj
T*
(   T = 1.5 * \(P/2\) * [ Psi_m * iqs + \(Ld - Lq\) * ids * iqs ].) Tj
T*
(   - Superior mechanical robustness for high-speed electric vehicle traction \(Tesla, Nissan Leaf\);) Tj
T*
(   wide field-weakening constant power speed range.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET

